PATCH 495: the remaining weapon-SPAWN methods 778a / 77cf / 7814 / 784a -- patch 429's 7745 defect, four more times.

The 7e29 far table (image 0x7e77, indexed by byte[di+0x91]<<1) selects the weapon spawn method:
0 -> 0f69:80b5 = 7745 (fixed by patch 429), 2 -> 778a, 4 -> 7814, 6 -> 77cf; 784a is the same idiom on
the dispense path.  All four carry the identical set of decompile defects:

  * the firer DI is a DGROUP NEAR OFFSET (7e29 passes it as param_4, or param_3 for 7814 / param_2 for
    784a) and was dereferenced as a host pointer -> SIGSEGV on the first shot;
  * the ammo counter is a WORD (`decw 0xaf(%di)` / 0xb3 / 0xb1; 784a's 0xb5 is a BYTE) read as 4-byte int;
  * b1df's returned projectile was DROPPED -- the asm is `call 1b1df ; mov si,di ; pop di`, so SI is the
    NEW object and DI the firer -- and Ghidra substituted the uninitialised `unaff_CS` pseudo-var for
    BOTH in the whole tail (b73b/b767/b6c9/9a50 and every [+0xa8]/[+0x3c]/[+0x92] store);
  * the clc/stc CF contract was lost.  7e29 reads it (g_fist_cf) to choose bf77 (spawn failed) over
    bf94 / the bf3c muzzle effect.

Two asm details specific to 7814: it is gated on `testw $0x7,[DGROUP:0x6cde]` (nonzero -> clc, no ammo
touched, and NO a265 aim call, unlike its siblings), and a b1df failure lands on the clc exit (0x17846),
not the stc one -- only the empty-magazine path (0x17848) sets CF.  784a's failure path plays the
a4a2(0x3031) cue with DI (the firer) still live.

This code was unreachable until patch 494 fixed the hull velocity decomposition: before it no unit ever
closed to firing range and 7e29 was entered 0 times in a 20000-tick AZER1 self-play.  With 494 the first
live engagement reaches it and UKRAINE3 faulted at 778a <- 7e29 <- 7c1d <- c0e5 <- c0ca <- 459a.
